+## Files NOT ported / deferred
+
+None. Every file listed in the patch summary has been touched. The only
+architectural shift is:
+
+- **`FlutterPlatformViews_Internal.mm` was refactored away in 3.41.6.** The
+  8-line patch hunk (WebKit import guard + `multipleTouchEnabled` guard +
+  `containsWebView` WKWebView-class guard) was applied to
+  `FlutterPlatformViews.mm` instead, which holds the equivalent code. **Marked
+  as ported cleanly** because the intent is fully preserved — just at a
+  different file path.
+
+## Known compile-risk areas to investigate next
+
+Priority-ordered list of things to watch for on first compile attempt:
+
+1. **DEPS fork mismatches** (highest risk). LibertyGlobal's
+   `flutter-tvos-dart@3.27.4` and `flutter-tvos-skia@3.27.4` have commit SHAs
+   that predate Flutter 3.41.6's expected dart/skia. Symptoms will likely be:
+   missing `_FlutterMergeBranchCommit` style symbols, unresolved Dart API
+   calls in `dart:ui`, or Skia C++ ABI mismatches. May need to either:
+   - upgrade the LibertyGlobal forks to match 3.41.6's dart/skia SHAs, or
+   - revert dart/skia in DEPS to upstream and accept any tvOS-specific fixes
+     from LibertyGlobal as additional local patches.
+
+2. **Impeller Metal feature-set fallbacks**. 3.41.6 assumes iOS 13+ (direct
+   `supportsFamily:` calls). Our tvOS branches call the older
+   `MTLFeatureSet_tvOS_GPUFamily*_v1` APIs which are deprecated. Compile may
+   warn; may need `API_DEPRECATED` opt-out pragma.
+
+3. **`UIStatusBarStyleDarkContent`** in `FlutterPlatformPlugin.mm`. Introduced
+   in iOS 13 — guarded in 3.41.6 but on tvOS the entire code path is
+   `#if`-disabled, so this should not compile on tvOS. Verify.
+
+4. **`FlutterPlatformPlugin.mm` `SetStatusBarHidden/Style` helpers**: 3.41.6
+   changed these from the old `APPLICATION_EXTENSION_API_ONLY` macro to
+   `FlutterSharedApplication`. The tvOS guards skip the entire helpers. Verify
+   no call site left dangling.
+
+5. **`accessibility_bridge.mm`** `childrenInHitTestOrder` field: the patch
+   assumes the 3.27.4 API. In 3.41.6 this field still exists on
+   `SemanticsObject`. Our tvOS branches don't set it (preserving the
+   patch's intent), which should be safe — verify no later code path asserts
+   its non-null-ness.
+
+6. **FlutterViewController.mm tvOS selectionView**: we call
+   `setNeedsFocusUpdate` / `updateFocusIfNeeded` in
+   `FlutterAccessibilitySelectionView` — both are tvOS-only UIKit APIs, so
+   the class file has no iOS-impacting code, but the `#import` in
+   `accessibility_bridge.mm` is unconditional. If someone builds the iOS
+   target from this worktree, the import will resolve but the class will
+   never be instantiated — should be OK, but verify.
+
+7. **`FlutterTextInputPlugin.h` `UIIndirectScribbleInteractionDelegate`
+   protocol conformance**: removed on tvOS. Verify no caller in the framework
+   tries to assign a plugin instance to a variable typed as the protocol.
+
+8. **`FlutterViewController.mm` `FlutterViewControllerHideHomeIndicator` /
+   `...ShowHomeIndicator` notification posts**: tvOS code paths in the
+   platform plugin (`setSystemChromeEnabledSystemUIMode:`) still try to post
+   these notifications; the observer side is disabled. Benign, but it's
+   worth cleaning up.
+
+9. **Test file build**: even though test sources are commented out in BUILD.gn,
+   our guards still need to compile successfully when anyone re-enables
+   individual tests on iOS. A mis-placed `#endif` would surface there.
+
+## Summary
+
+- 39 of 39 patch files addressed.
+- 3 files ported with TODOs (all test files; iOS tests still build fine).
+- 0 files deferred.
+- Biggest architectural adaptation: Impeller Metal backend (simplified in
+  3.41.6 — applied patch *intent* rather than textual hunks) and
+  FlutterPlatformViews refactor.
+- Branch: `tvos-port` in the local engine worktree.
